WEBVTT

00:00:10.343 --> 00:00:12.311
Now these are delicious.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:15.614
Uh, leave some
for the rest of us.

00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:17.650
Hey, I'm eating for two.

00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:20.944
Great party, Neelix.

00:00:21.021 --> 00:00:23.819
Everybody seems
to be enjoying it.

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:25.187
Yeah, except the Doc.

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:32.498
Those are for eating,
not scanning.

00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:33.827
What exactly are they?

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:35.162
Cheese pirogies.

00:00:35.235 --> 00:00:36.793
Zefram Cochrane's favorite.

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:39.464
They have absolutely
no nutritional value.

00:00:39.539 --> 00:00:41.097
This is a party, Doctor.

00:00:41.174 --> 00:00:43.301
Sometimes you have to
forget about nutrition.

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:45.173
You could include
a vitamin supplement

00:00:45.245 --> 00:00:46.507
when you replicate.

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:49.639
Replicate? I made them myself.

00:00:49.716 --> 00:00:52.276
You two have outdone yourselves.

00:00:52.352 --> 00:00:55.378
I've never seen First Contact
Day celebrated quite like this.

00:00:55.455 --> 00:00:57.719
When I was your age,
all it meant was a day off

00:00:57.791 --> 00:00:59.383
from school.

00:00:59.459 --> 00:01:01.825
Well, Neelix and I thought
we should make it more fun.

00:01:01.895 --> 00:01:03.226
Well, you certainly succeeded.

00:01:03.296 --> 00:01:05.491
When is Commander Tuvok
making his presentation?

00:01:05.565 --> 00:01:08.159
Well, now's as good
a time as any.

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:10.498
Captain.

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:13.471
Uh, may I have everyone's
attention, please?

00:01:14.741 --> 00:01:16.936
In honor of the 315th

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:20.946
anniversary of his ancestors'
arrival on Earth,

00:01:21.047 --> 00:01:24.312
I've asked Mr. Tuvok to
recite the first words

00:01:24.384 --> 00:01:25.578
spoken to humans by a Vulcan.

00:01:27.053 --> 00:01:28.213
Commander?

00:01:30.056 --> 00:01:31.546
Is this really necessary?

00:01:31.624 --> 00:01:33.421
You promised.

00:01:35.061 --> 00:01:37.188
Very well.

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:39.094
Live long and prosper.

00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:40.257
Ah.

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:45.431
And now, for some more

00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:48.201
of Zefram Cochrane's
favorite music.

00:01:59.619 --> 00:02:02.247
Hey, come on, Mr. Vulcan.

00:02:02.322 --> 00:02:05.086
Vulcans do not dance.

00:02:05.158 --> 00:02:06.921
But it's tradition.

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:09.085
There is no tradition,
Mr. Neelix.

00:02:09.162 --> 00:02:11.687
This ceremony
is entirely your invention.

00:02:11.764 --> 00:02:14.130
This is an official
ship function, Commander.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:17.294
Don't make me order you
to dance.

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:18.632
Sorry to interrupt,

00:02:18.705 --> 00:02:20.070
but I've got
some interesting news.

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:21.607
Neelix, you might want
to hear this.

00:02:21.674 --> 00:02:22.834
Huh?

00:02:24.744 --> 00:02:27.304
Long-range sensors have detected
several hundred life signs

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:31.646
approximately 4.9
light-years away.

00:02:31.718 --> 00:02:32.707
They're Talaxian.

00:04:33.506 --> 00:04:34.598
Are we there yet?

00:04:34.674 --> 00:04:35.606
Not exactly.

00:04:36.676 --> 00:04:38.735
The life signs appear
to be coming from inside

00:04:38.811 --> 00:04:39.937
that asteroid field.

00:04:40.046 --> 00:04:41.138
From a ship?

00:04:41.214 --> 00:04:42.875
We are not detecting
any vessels.

00:04:44.217 --> 00:04:45.809
No response from hails?

00:04:45.885 --> 00:04:47.147
Not yet.

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:50.155
I hope they're all right.

00:04:50.223 --> 00:04:51.815
There's a lot of interference.

00:04:51.891 --> 00:04:54.621
Maybe they haven't received
our transmissions.

00:04:54.694 --> 00:04:56.127
Can we move in any closer?

00:04:56.195 --> 00:04:59.323
Voyager is too big
to maneuver safely in there.

00:04:59.399 --> 00:05:01.094
We could take the Flyer.

00:05:03.936 --> 00:05:05.836
It wouldn't have hurt you
to do a few steps.

00:05:05.905 --> 00:05:08.237
I am trying to concentrate
on the shields, Mr. Neelix.

00:05:08.308 --> 00:05:09.900
I think you were just afraid.

00:05:09.976 --> 00:05:11.443
That's absurd.

00:05:11.511 --> 00:05:12.671
It's understandable.

00:05:12.745 --> 00:05:14.838
There were a lot of people
watching.

00:05:14.914 --> 00:05:17.178
Vulcans don't experience fear.

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:20.242
I'm going to make it
my personal mission

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:21.787
to get you to dance
at least once

00:05:21.854 --> 00:05:22.843
before we reach Earth.

00:05:22.922 --> 00:05:25.516
Then I suggest you find
a more productive hobby.

00:05:25.591 --> 00:05:27.889
If you two
don't stop it, I'm going

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:29.757
to come back there
and separate you.

00:05:32.298 --> 00:05:33.925
I've localized the life signs.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:37.492
Bearing 108 mark 26.

00:05:37.570 --> 00:05:40.198
They appear to be inside
a large asteroid.

00:05:40.273 --> 00:05:41.205
Inside?

00:05:42.508 --> 00:05:43.805
What was that?

00:05:43.876 --> 00:05:45.173
A thermalyte explosive.

00:05:45.244 --> 00:05:46.643
30.6 kilometers to port.

00:05:46.713 --> 00:05:48.681
I'm detecting
another projectile,

00:05:48.748 --> 00:05:50.113
heading directly toward us.

00:05:50.183 --> 00:05:52.344
Evasive maneuvers.

00:05:57.090 --> 00:05:58.751
We've lost shields.

00:05:58.825 --> 00:06:00.952
Main propulsion is off-line.

00:06:01.027 --> 00:06:03.086
We're going to have
to make an emergency landing.

00:06:03.162 --> 00:06:04.754
Where?

00:06:04.831 --> 00:06:06.822
The Talaxians' asteroid
is the closest.

00:06:06.899 --> 00:06:09.800
The surface is covered
with craters, ice fields.

00:06:12.772 --> 00:06:13.898
We don't have a choice.

00:06:14.006 --> 00:06:15.405
Hold on.

00:06:39.365 --> 00:06:40.491
Problem?

00:06:40.566 --> 00:06:42.227
We've lost contact
with the away team.

00:06:42.301 --> 00:06:44.394
I also detected some
unusual energy discharges

00:06:44.470 --> 00:06:45.437
in the asteroid field.

00:06:45.505 --> 00:06:46.529
What kind of discharges?

00:06:46.606 --> 00:06:47.573
It's difficult to tell

00:06:47.640 --> 00:06:49.631
because of the interference,
but they appear

00:06:49.709 --> 00:06:51.199
to be thermalytic explosions.

00:06:51.277 --> 00:06:53.302
I believe several of them
were in close

00:06:53.379 --> 00:06:55.711
proximity to the Flyer.

00:06:55.782 --> 00:06:56.874
Source?

00:06:56.949 --> 00:06:58.416
Unknown.

00:07:00.753 --> 00:07:02.744
We'll need
to send a rescue team.

00:07:02.822 --> 00:07:03.880
Work with B'Elanna.

00:07:03.990 --> 00:07:06.083
Try to modify the shields
on one of the shuttles

00:07:06.159 --> 00:07:07.717
to withstand these explosions.

00:07:18.104 --> 00:07:20.072
Stay still.

00:07:21.441 --> 00:07:23.466
Don't worry.
It's not serious.

00:07:25.445 --> 00:07:27.470
Am I inside the asteroid?

00:07:27.547 --> 00:07:28.707
Yes.

00:07:28.781 --> 00:07:30.214
This is my home.

00:07:30.283 --> 00:07:32.444
Where are my friends?

00:07:32.518 --> 00:07:33.780
If you mean the aliens

00:07:33.853 --> 00:07:36.481
who were on the ship with you,
they're safe.

00:07:38.124 --> 00:07:39.614
I'd like to see them.

00:07:39.692 --> 00:07:41.489
You need to rest.

00:07:46.132 --> 00:07:48.430
What were you doing
in the asteroid field?

00:07:50.036 --> 00:07:51.503
Looking for you.

00:07:52.805 --> 00:07:56.070
Well, not you s-specifically,

00:07:56.142 --> 00:07:59.202
but my ship
detected Talaxians.

00:07:59.278 --> 00:08:02.509
I haven't come across
any in years, so...

00:08:03.749 --> 00:08:05.239
I'm sorry.

00:08:05.318 --> 00:08:06.979
I'm Neelix.

00:08:07.053 --> 00:08:08.680
Dexa.

00:08:08.754 --> 00:08:11.552
I had an uncle named Neelix.

00:08:13.292 --> 00:08:15.624
Are there other Talaxians
on your ship?

00:08:15.695 --> 00:08:17.185
I'm the only one.

00:08:17.263 --> 00:08:20.027
Why are you living
with aliens?

00:08:20.099 --> 00:08:21.862
They're my friends.

00:08:21.934 --> 00:08:24.698
Did you receive our hails?

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:25.862
Yes.

00:08:25.938 --> 00:08:27.030
Why didn't you respond?

00:08:27.106 --> 00:08:30.269
We avoid
contact with outsiders.

00:08:32.445 --> 00:08:34.413
We were attacked.

00:08:35.481 --> 00:08:37.847
There were explosions.

00:08:37.917 --> 00:08:39.043
Did you?

00:08:39.118 --> 00:08:40.710
No.

00:08:40.786 --> 00:08:42.686
We're not violent.

00:08:42.755 --> 00:08:44.120
Who fired at us?

00:08:44.190 --> 00:08:45.919
No one fired at you.

00:08:46.025 --> 00:08:48.186
There are miners
who use explosive charges

00:08:48.261 --> 00:08:49.728
to break apart the asteroids,

00:08:49.795 --> 00:08:53.390
so they can collect minerals
from the debris.

00:08:53.466 --> 00:08:55.058
I wish we'd known.

00:08:55.134 --> 00:08:56.761
Why were you carrying weapons?

00:08:56.836 --> 00:09:00.033
It's standard procedure
for an away mission.

00:09:03.075 --> 00:09:04.269
Hello.

00:09:04.343 --> 00:09:05.810
What's your name?

00:09:05.878 --> 00:09:07.004
Brax.

00:09:07.079 --> 00:09:08.341
What's yours?

00:09:08.414 --> 00:09:10.348
I told you not to come in here.

00:09:10.416 --> 00:09:11.974
I just wanted to see him.

00:09:12.051 --> 00:09:14.519
You're supposed
to be helping Oxilon.

00:09:14.587 --> 00:09:16.851
He doesn't look
dangerous to me.

00:09:20.092 --> 00:09:22.151
I think you have the wrong idea
about us.

00:09:22.228 --> 00:09:24.924
I'm not supposed to be
talking to you at all.

00:09:27.333 --> 00:09:28.265
I'm feeling better.

00:09:28.334 --> 00:09:30.598
I-I'd like
to see my friends now.

00:09:33.406 --> 00:09:34.771
What are you doing?

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:37.172
I've been told
not to let you leave.

00:09:47.987 --> 00:09:49.318
Harry?

00:09:49.388 --> 00:09:50.480
Still no response to hails.

00:09:50.556 --> 00:09:51.716
Janeway to the Shuttle Bay.

00:09:51.791 --> 00:09:53.349
Go ahead, Captain.

00:09:53.426 --> 00:09:55.189
What's the status
of the shield modifications?

00:09:55.261 --> 00:09:57.729
Lieutenant Torres and I will be
finished in a few minutes.

00:09:57.797 --> 00:09:59.355
Good.

00:09:59.432 --> 00:10:01.024
Take an away team and find them.

00:10:03.169 --> 00:10:05.535
Captain, there's a ship
approaching from astern.

00:10:05.605 --> 00:10:06.799
We're being hailed.

00:10:06.872 --> 00:10:08.703
On screen.

00:10:09.709 --> 00:10:11.939
Identify yourselves.

00:10:12.044 --> 00:10:13.238
I'm Captain Janeway

00:10:13.312 --> 00:10:15.280
of the Federation
Starship Voyager.

00:10:15.348 --> 00:10:17.441
Commander Nocona.

00:10:17.516 --> 00:10:19.040
This is our asteroid field.

00:10:20.419 --> 00:10:22.284
We weren't aware of that.

00:10:22.355 --> 00:10:24.050
Now you are.

00:10:24.123 --> 00:10:27.183
We lost one of our shuttles
inside the field.

00:10:27.259 --> 00:10:30.057
We're preparing
to send a rescue team.

00:10:30.129 --> 00:10:32.563
All the resources belong to us.

00:10:32.632 --> 00:10:33.963
We're not interested
in the resources.

00:10:34.066 --> 00:10:35.363
We were only trying
to make contact

00:10:35.434 --> 00:10:36.366
with the Talaxians.

00:10:36.435 --> 00:10:39.461
What's your interest in them?

00:10:39.538 --> 00:10:41.699
One of my crewmen is from Talax.

00:10:41.774 --> 00:10:43.867
He was eager
to meet some of his people.

00:10:43.943 --> 00:10:45.672
You should have requested
permission

00:10:45.745 --> 00:10:47.576
before sending in a shuttle.

00:10:47.647 --> 00:10:49.808
We have a mining operation
in progress.

00:10:49.882 --> 00:10:52.976
Does that explain
the explosions we detected?

00:10:53.052 --> 00:10:54.815
Mining charges.

00:10:54.887 --> 00:10:57.412
We'd appreciate it
if you'd stop using them,

00:10:57.490 --> 00:10:58.923
until we can get our people out.

00:10:58.991 --> 00:11:00.083
I'm sorry.

00:11:00.159 --> 00:11:02.354
We're on a strict deadline.

00:11:02.428 --> 00:11:06.125
But I'll conduct a search
for your crew.

00:11:06.198 --> 00:11:08.928
If they need help,
we'll provide it.

00:11:09.068 --> 00:11:10.899
That's kind of you.

00:11:10.970 --> 00:11:13.905
But we're prepared to go in
and get them ourselves.

00:11:13.973 --> 00:11:18.672
I cannot guarantee your safety
if you enter the asteroid field.

00:11:18.744 --> 00:11:20.109
Stay here.

00:11:20.179 --> 00:11:23.012
We'll contact you
when we find your people.

00:11:35.294 --> 00:11:37.854
I don't think
you're supposed to be here.

00:11:37.930 --> 00:11:39.557
This is my home.

00:11:39.632 --> 00:11:41.759
You can't tell me what to do.

00:11:41.834 --> 00:11:44.098
No, of course not.

00:11:44.170 --> 00:11:46.070
I just don't want you
to get in trouble.

00:11:47.139 --> 00:11:49.403
Is that a model ship?

00:11:49.475 --> 00:11:51.739
What's it called?

00:11:51.811 --> 00:11:53.972
How about The Two-Tailed
Talchok?

00:11:55.347 --> 00:11:57.076
The Fur Fly?

00:11:59.985 --> 00:12:02.283
The ship I come from
is called Voyager.

00:12:02.354 --> 00:12:03.878
Is it big?

00:12:05.357 --> 00:12:06.381
And fast.

00:12:06.459 --> 00:12:08.324
Can I see it?

00:12:09.829 --> 00:12:11.456
I think it would be
a little difficult

00:12:11.530 --> 00:12:13.930
to take you there
while I'm stuck here.

00:12:13.999 --> 00:12:16.934
But if your mother
would let me out...

00:12:18.204 --> 00:12:19.228
That's her.

00:12:19.305 --> 00:12:21.170
You better hide.

00:12:21.240 --> 00:12:22.673
You won't tell her I'm here?

00:12:22.742 --> 00:12:24.334
No, of course not.

00:12:33.819 --> 00:12:38.449
Neelix, this is Oxilon
our Council Regent.

00:12:38.524 --> 00:12:40.287
I wish I could say it
was nice to meet you,

00:12:40.359 --> 00:12:43.226
but this wasn't exactly
the welcome I was expecting.

00:12:43.295 --> 00:12:44.421
You're free to go now.

00:12:53.339 --> 00:12:54.601
What about my friends?

00:12:54.673 --> 00:12:56.766
We've determined
they aren't hostile.

00:12:56.842 --> 00:12:58.469
They've been treated
for their injuries

00:12:58.544 --> 00:12:59.670
and asked to leave.

00:12:59.745 --> 00:13:02.612
They're aboard your shuttle
making repairs.

00:13:02.681 --> 00:13:03.648
I'll take you there.

00:13:05.084 --> 00:13:08.918
Well, now that everything
has been cleared up,

00:13:09.054 --> 00:13:12.023
maybe we could talk...

00:13:12.091 --> 00:13:13.854
get to know each other
a little?

00:13:16.929 --> 00:13:18.453
If you'd like.

00:13:18.531 --> 00:13:20.897
My friends, too?

00:13:20.966 --> 00:13:22.558
I'm sorry.

00:13:22.635 --> 00:13:23.897
Why not?

00:13:23.969 --> 00:13:25.402
We've learned from experience

00:13:25.471 --> 00:13:26.631
to keep to ourselves.

00:13:28.374 --> 00:13:29.739
Well, if they're not welcome,

00:13:29.809 --> 00:13:31.538
I'm not staying, either.

00:13:33.245 --> 00:13:34.735
That's your choice.

00:13:42.121 --> 00:13:44.146
I know Oxilon seems
overly cautious,

00:13:44.223 --> 00:13:46.953
but we're not used
to having visitors.

00:13:47.059 --> 00:13:49.584
How many of you live here?

00:13:51.096 --> 00:13:53.564
Close to 500.

00:13:53.632 --> 00:13:55.497
All of our homes are connected
to the central

00:13:55.568 --> 00:13:57.900
cavern by tunnels and lifts.

00:13:57.970 --> 00:13:59.198
They allow us to move easily

00:13:59.271 --> 00:14:01.364
from one section
of the asteroid to another.

00:14:02.908 --> 00:14:06.867
It must have taken years
to build all of this.

00:14:06.946 --> 00:14:08.470
Almost five.

00:14:08.547 --> 00:14:10.515
It still isn't finished.

00:14:12.184 --> 00:14:15.085
...group five, report
to the lower level...

00:14:15.154 --> 00:14:16.678
Where did the technology
come from?

00:14:16.755 --> 00:14:19.781
We arrived here
with a caravan of six ships.

00:14:19.859 --> 00:14:21.520
We disassembled
all but one of them

00:14:21.594 --> 00:14:23.323
and modified their components.

00:14:23.395 --> 00:14:26.057
We converted torpedo launchers
to blast away rock

00:14:26.131 --> 00:14:27.598
and excavate these tunnels.

00:14:27.666 --> 00:14:29.964
These conduits run
into the asteroid's core.

00:14:31.303 --> 00:14:34.067
We use geothermal energy
to melt the ice that covers most

00:14:34.139 --> 00:14:35.936
of the outer surface.
It provides us

00:14:36.041 --> 00:14:38.066
with oxygen and water.

00:14:38.143 --> 00:14:41.943
Who'd have imagined all of this
inside an asteroid?

00:14:46.252 --> 00:14:48.948
Your son seems like
a wonderful boy.

00:14:49.088 --> 00:14:50.487
How would you know?

00:14:50.556 --> 00:14:52.547
You only met him
for a few seconds.

00:14:53.893 --> 00:14:57.226
True, but I'm a quick
judge of character.

00:14:58.297 --> 00:15:01.494
He came to see you
while I was out, didn't he?

00:15:03.302 --> 00:15:05.236
You can't blame him
for being curious.

00:15:05.304 --> 00:15:08.637
Hmm.
He's a lot like his father...

00:15:08.707 --> 00:15:10.538
no fear.

00:15:10.609 --> 00:15:12.736
I'd like to meet your husband.

00:15:15.080 --> 00:15:16.638
He's dead.

00:15:16.715 --> 00:15:19.343
I'm sorry.

00:15:19.418 --> 00:15:20.476
I didn't mean to...

00:15:20.552 --> 00:15:21.849
It's... it's all right.

00:15:21.921 --> 00:15:23.650
You didn't know.

00:15:28.594 --> 00:15:29.561
Neelix.

00:15:30.829 --> 00:15:31.921
Are you all right?

00:15:32.031 --> 00:15:33.555
I'm fine.

00:15:33.632 --> 00:15:38.467
Dexa, this is Lieutenant Paris
and Commander Tuvok.

00:15:38.537 --> 00:15:40.368
Thanks for bringing him back.

00:15:40.439 --> 00:15:41.804
We were getting worried.

00:15:43.709 --> 00:15:46.007
It was nice to meet you.

00:15:54.620 --> 00:15:57.521
So, what can I do to help?

00:15:57.589 --> 00:16:00.786
Well, you can give me a hand
with this plasma manifold.

00:16:03.462 --> 00:16:05.293
How did it go?

00:16:05.364 --> 00:16:06.888
Well, uh, they didn't exactly

00:16:06.999 --> 00:16:08.466
send out a welcoming committee,

00:16:08.534 --> 00:16:10.195
but I'm sure
they have their reasons.

00:16:13.172 --> 00:16:15.402
I guess my expectations
were a little high.

00:16:17.443 --> 00:16:20.469
I regret that you didn't have
a more fulfilling experience.

00:16:20.546 --> 00:16:22.104
That's nice of you to say,
Commander,

00:16:22.181 --> 00:16:23.910
but it wasn't a complete
waste of time.

00:16:24.016 --> 00:16:26.280
I got to meet some
of my people again...

00:16:26.352 --> 00:16:28.445
even if it was a short visit.

00:16:28.520 --> 00:16:30.920
Who knows?

00:16:31.023 --> 00:16:35.255
It's probably the last time
I'll ever see another Talaxian.

00:16:43.869 --> 00:16:45.564
Good work.

00:16:45.637 --> 00:16:47.332
Now we need to run a systems...

00:16:47.406 --> 00:16:49.465
Intruder alert.

00:16:49.541 --> 00:16:52.510
At least we know internal
sensors are working.

00:17:10.763 --> 00:17:12.788
Brax.

00:17:13.832 --> 00:17:15.356
You know him?

00:17:15.434 --> 00:17:17.766
We're old friends.

00:17:17.836 --> 00:17:20.896
You said you'd take me
to see Voyager.

00:17:21.006 --> 00:17:23.907
I don't think
your mother would approve.

00:17:23.976 --> 00:17:26.274
You won't tell her
I was here, will you?

00:17:26.345 --> 00:17:28.142
Here?

00:17:28.213 --> 00:17:30.875
Why, I have no idea
what you're talking about.

00:17:32.051 --> 00:17:33.746
I'll be right back.

00:17:37.122 --> 00:17:39.420
Three days isn't nearly
enough time for us

00:17:39.491 --> 00:17:41.118
to dismantle all our equipment.

00:17:41.193 --> 00:17:43.491
You should have begun
the first time we asked.

00:17:43.562 --> 00:17:44.893
We can't wait any longer.

00:17:44.963 --> 00:17:46.863
Demolition of the asteroid
is going to start

00:17:46.932 --> 00:17:48.832
whether you're here or not.

00:17:48.901 --> 00:17:50.095
You'd kill us?

00:17:50.169 --> 00:17:52.603
We don't want to hurt anyone.

00:17:52.671 --> 00:17:54.935
But our patience has run out.

00:17:55.040 --> 00:17:57.065
We've only got one ship.

00:17:57.142 --> 00:17:59.474
There won't be enough room
for any of our belongings.

00:17:59.545 --> 00:18:00.637
It's not our fault

00:18:00.712 --> 00:18:02.612
you took apart
your other vessels.

00:18:02.681 --> 00:18:04.273
You can't do this.

00:18:04.349 --> 00:18:05.441
Dex, don't provoke him.

00:18:05.517 --> 00:18:07.178
Where are we supposed to go?

00:18:07.252 --> 00:18:09.413
I'm sure
you'll find a home somewhere.

00:18:09.488 --> 00:18:10.750
This is our home!

00:18:12.458 --> 00:18:13.925
You have no right to make us go.

00:18:16.728 --> 00:18:18.286
Leave her alone!

00:18:20.732 --> 00:18:22.700
Bring him here!

00:18:23.869 --> 00:18:24.801
Don't touch him!

00:18:24.870 --> 00:18:27.202
Are you going to stop me?

00:18:35.347 --> 00:18:38.316
You've said what you've come
to say, and now,

00:18:38.383 --> 00:18:40.283
I suggest you leave.

00:18:42.121 --> 00:18:46.080
You have three days to evacuate.

00:19:00.172 --> 00:19:03.300
You can see now why we're
suspicious of outsiders.

00:19:03.375 --> 00:19:05.070
Thank you
for protecting the boy,

00:19:05.144 --> 00:19:08.636
but I'm afraid your actions
might make things worse.

00:19:08.714 --> 00:19:10.272
How could they get any worse?

00:19:10.349 --> 00:19:12.214
Fighting back has
never done anything

00:19:12.284 --> 00:19:13.615
but cause us more trouble.

00:19:13.685 --> 00:19:15.482
And what has running
away ever done for us?

00:19:15.554 --> 00:19:17.249
- It's kept us alive.
- Maybe it's time

00:19:17.322 --> 00:19:19.882
we stayed
and defended ourselves.

00:19:19.958 --> 00:19:21.550
Will you help us?

00:19:23.395 --> 00:19:24.623
I agree with Oxilon.

00:19:24.696 --> 00:19:26.561
Fighting isn't the answer...

00:19:26.632 --> 00:19:28.759
but I'll try to help.

00:19:28.834 --> 00:19:30.597
How?

00:19:30.669 --> 00:19:31.795
Well, uh...

00:19:31.870 --> 00:19:33.895
we could talk to my Captain,

00:19:33.972 --> 00:19:36.805
and maybe she can negotiate
with the miners,

00:19:36.875 --> 00:19:39.400
uh, get them to agree
to let you stay.

00:19:39.478 --> 00:19:40.911
Your Captain would be
willing to do that?

00:19:41.013 --> 00:19:45.006
The best thing would be for you
to come to Voyager...

00:19:45.083 --> 00:19:47.017
talk to her yourself.

00:19:47.085 --> 00:19:48.245
I want to go, too.

00:19:48.320 --> 00:19:50.185
Shh, Brax.

00:19:50.255 --> 00:19:51.552
Why don't you both come?

00:19:51.623 --> 00:19:53.090
I've seen your home.

00:19:53.158 --> 00:19:55.285
I'd like you to see mine.

00:20:02.367 --> 00:20:04.267
Commander Chakotay.

00:20:04.336 --> 00:20:08.067
I'd like you to meet
Dexa... and Brax.

00:20:08.140 --> 00:20:09.437
Welcome to the Bridge.

00:20:09.508 --> 00:20:11.533
And this is Ensign Kim.

00:20:17.249 --> 00:20:18.682
What's this?

00:20:18.750 --> 00:20:21.651
This... is an
engineering station.

00:20:21.720 --> 00:20:24.484
And over there is Tactical.

00:20:24.556 --> 00:20:27.081
And down there is the Helm.

00:20:27.159 --> 00:20:31.892
And this... is
the Captain's chair.

00:20:31.964 --> 00:20:33.955
Which station is yours?

00:20:34.099 --> 00:20:35.123
Well, actually, I don't have

00:20:35.200 --> 00:20:36.963
a specific...
See, I'm-I'm

00:20:37.035 --> 00:20:38.263
more of a, uh...

00:20:38.337 --> 00:20:40.862
Neelix does too many things
to have just one station.

00:20:40.939 --> 00:20:42.907
He's our... Ambassador,

00:20:42.975 --> 00:20:44.806
- Morale Officer.
- Trade Negotiator.

00:20:44.876 --> 00:20:46.400
Without a doubt,

00:20:46.478 --> 00:20:48.469
he's the most versatile
member of our crew.

00:20:52.618 --> 00:20:55.086
As you can see, our sensors
are extremely precise.

00:20:55.153 --> 00:20:57.917
We can scan for life signs
light-years away.

00:20:57.990 --> 00:20:59.787
That's how we found you.

00:20:59.858 --> 00:21:02.418
I have something else
that may interest you.

00:21:05.664 --> 00:21:07.359
What is it?

00:21:07.432 --> 00:21:09.559
Talax...

00:21:09.635 --> 00:21:11.694
You can scan that far away?

00:21:11.770 --> 00:21:13.931
No. This image is
from our database.

00:21:14.006 --> 00:21:17.032
It's as beautiful as I remember.

00:21:18.610 --> 00:21:21.204
There's the Godo Mountain Range.

00:21:21.280 --> 00:21:23.214
And the Axiana Lakes.

00:21:23.282 --> 00:21:25.648
That was always one
of my favorite places.

00:21:25.717 --> 00:21:27.708
Mine, too.

00:21:27.786 --> 00:21:30.550
Why don't we
just go back to Talax?

00:21:30.622 --> 00:21:32.249
We could live there.

00:21:32.324 --> 00:21:35.191
It's still controlled
by the Haakonians.

00:21:35.260 --> 00:21:37.694
They don't treat
Talaxians very well.

00:21:37.763 --> 00:21:38.957
That's why we left.

00:21:39.097 --> 00:21:40.792
Maybe Neelix could go with us,

00:21:40.866 --> 00:21:42.766
and we could fight them.

00:21:42.834 --> 00:21:44.563
Take the planet back.

00:21:44.636 --> 00:21:46.695
If tomorrow's
negotiations go well,

00:21:46.772 --> 00:21:50.071
you won't have to go anywhere.

00:21:52.844 --> 00:21:55.813
Next stop... Engineering.

00:21:55.881 --> 00:21:58.111
The warp core.

00:21:58.183 --> 00:21:59.810
Neelix.

00:21:59.885 --> 00:22:01.443
Naomi.

00:22:01.520 --> 00:22:02.612
I'm sorry.

00:22:02.688 --> 00:22:04.280
I forgot all about
our Kadis-Kot game.

00:22:04.356 --> 00:22:06.916
That's all right.
I know you're busy.

00:22:07.059 --> 00:22:08.617
I just wanted
to meet your friends.

00:22:08.694 --> 00:22:11.254
Of course. Dexa, Brax...

00:22:11.330 --> 00:22:12.854
this is my goddaughter, Naomi.

00:22:12.931 --> 00:22:14.398
Hi.

00:22:14.466 --> 00:22:15.626
You live on a beautiful ship.

00:22:15.701 --> 00:22:17.259
Thanks.

00:22:17.336 --> 00:22:19.702
Maybe Brax would like
to go to the holodeck.

00:22:19.771 --> 00:22:20.829
That's a great idea.

00:22:20.906 --> 00:22:22.897
Lieutenant Paris has
a new program.

00:22:22.974 --> 00:22:25.067
"Invaders from
the Ninth Dimension."

00:22:25.143 --> 00:22:26.576
Sounds scary.

00:22:26.645 --> 00:22:27.942
Very.

00:22:28.080 --> 00:22:29.741
What's a holodeck?

00:22:29.815 --> 00:22:30.941
Neelix is right.

00:22:31.049 --> 00:22:33.108
Might be too scary for you.

00:22:33.185 --> 00:22:34.550
I'm not afraid.

00:22:34.619 --> 00:22:37.087
Can I?

00:22:42.661 --> 00:22:45.095
You're lucky
to have found these people.

00:22:48.033 --> 00:22:50.331
They obviously think
a great deal of you.

00:22:50.402 --> 00:22:52.063
The feeling's mutual.

00:23:05.050 --> 00:23:07.917
To the Axiana Lakes.

00:23:12.791 --> 00:23:14.588
It really is delicious.

00:23:14.659 --> 00:23:17.184
I've been saving it
for 15 years.

00:23:17.262 --> 00:23:19.594
I wasn't sure I'd ever open it.

00:23:22.701 --> 00:23:24.430
But tonight...

00:23:24.503 --> 00:23:26.903
seemed like the right occasion.

00:23:31.977 --> 00:23:33.911
Would you like some more...

00:23:33.979 --> 00:23:35.071
taga cake?

00:23:35.147 --> 00:23:37.479
A-A little, please.

00:23:39.151 --> 00:23:41.745
I haven't had this in years.

00:23:41.820 --> 00:23:43.082
I'm glad you like it.

00:23:43.155 --> 00:23:44.087
Mmm.

00:23:44.156 --> 00:23:46.124
It's a family recipe.

00:23:46.191 --> 00:23:48.022
You're a good cook.

00:23:49.094 --> 00:23:50.584
I haven't seen Brax

00:23:50.662 --> 00:23:52.653
this happy
since his father was alive.

00:23:55.901 --> 00:23:57.801
How did he?

00:23:57.869 --> 00:23:59.063
I'm sorry.

00:23:59.137 --> 00:24:01.435
You probably don't
want to talk about it.

00:24:01.506 --> 00:24:03.997
I don't mind.

00:24:04.075 --> 00:24:06.771
We'd settled on a planet
called Phanos.

00:24:06.845 --> 00:24:08.608
There was a lot
of unoccupied territory,

00:24:08.680 --> 00:24:11.740
but the government restricted us
to a very small area.

00:24:11.817 --> 00:24:12.806
Why?

00:24:12.884 --> 00:24:14.784
They said it was a quarantine,

00:24:14.853 --> 00:24:17.788
to protect the population
from "alien diseases."

00:24:17.856 --> 00:24:20.450
But it was just an excuse.

00:24:20.525 --> 00:24:21.651
We were outsiders.

00:24:21.726 --> 00:24:23.626
They didn't want us
mixing with their people.

00:24:25.597 --> 00:24:27.121
It wasn't long before
we realized

00:24:27.199 --> 00:24:28.427
we didn't have enough land

00:24:28.500 --> 00:24:30.695
to grow what we needed
to feed ourselves.

00:24:32.304 --> 00:24:37.765
Oxilon said we'd just have
to conserve our resources,

00:24:37.843 --> 00:24:41.836
but my husband was tired
of being told what to do.

00:24:41.913 --> 00:24:46.373
So, he started farming
outside the restricted zone.

00:24:46.451 --> 00:24:47.748
They didn't like that.

00:24:47.819 --> 00:24:50.652
A security patrol
confronted him.

00:24:50.722 --> 00:24:53.418
He told them he had to provide
for his family,

00:24:53.492 --> 00:24:55.357
that he wasn't afraid of them.

00:24:55.427 --> 00:24:57.725
There was a fight;
he was killed.

00:24:59.464 --> 00:25:01.329
I'm sorry.

00:25:01.399 --> 00:25:04.596
After that, we came here.

00:25:04.669 --> 00:25:06.899
We thought
we'd finally found a place

00:25:06.972 --> 00:25:08.769
where no one would bother us.

00:25:08.840 --> 00:25:11.206
Maybe this time
it'll be different.

00:25:11.276 --> 00:25:13.039
Maybe.

00:25:15.213 --> 00:25:16.646
But even if it isn't...

00:25:19.050 --> 00:25:21.177
thank you for trying.

00:25:28.860 --> 00:25:30.794
I should get
a good night's sleep,

00:25:30.862 --> 00:25:35.356
if I'm going to be my best
at the negotiations tomorrow.

00:25:41.006 --> 00:25:42.701
Uh, Neelix?

00:25:44.809 --> 00:25:48.301
It's been a wonderful day.

00:25:57.622 --> 00:26:01.183
Isn't there enough to mine here,
without destroying their home?

00:26:01.259 --> 00:26:04.057
Their home contains
more than 30 percent

00:26:04.129 --> 00:26:05.994
of the field's ore.

00:26:06.064 --> 00:26:07.759
Without that asteroid...

00:26:07.832 --> 00:26:10.392
the operation isn't
worth the expense.

00:26:10.468 --> 00:26:14.268
Would you be open
to some kind of compensation?

00:26:14.339 --> 00:26:17.740
All we want are the minerals.

00:26:17.809 --> 00:26:19.902
And you'd kill us to get them.

00:26:20.045 --> 00:26:21.034
Wait.

00:26:22.581 --> 00:26:24.742
The Talaxians have found a way

00:26:24.816 --> 00:26:27.614
to produce a lot
of geothermal energy.

00:26:27.686 --> 00:26:30.814
Maybe they could
share it with you.

00:26:33.158 --> 00:26:35.149
What do you mean "share"?

00:26:37.295 --> 00:26:41.254
You could convert it into fuel
to power your ships.

00:26:41.333 --> 00:26:45.861
The energy they generate isn't
compatible with our technology.

00:26:45.937 --> 00:26:48.428
We'd be willing to help you
make the modifications.

00:26:48.506 --> 00:26:50.474
We have quotas to meet.

00:26:50.542 --> 00:26:52.533
We don't have time for that.

00:26:52.611 --> 00:26:53.942
Commander,

00:26:54.012 --> 00:26:56.742
the future of more than
500 people is at stake here.

00:27:00.819 --> 00:27:03.310
And once, there was
a transporter accident.

00:27:03.388 --> 00:27:05.754
Neelix and Commander Tuvok
got combined

00:27:05.824 --> 00:27:07.553
to make a completely
different person.

00:27:07.626 --> 00:27:09.059
Really?

00:27:09.127 --> 00:27:12.062
You don't think I could make up
a story like that, do you?

00:27:12.130 --> 00:27:14.360
Hello, Neelix.

00:27:14.432 --> 00:27:16.093
Do you want to play Kadis-Kot?

00:27:16.167 --> 00:27:18.431
Maybe later.

00:27:29.080 --> 00:27:31.571
I knew it wouldn't work.

00:27:31.650 --> 00:27:33.675
We did get them
to make a small concession.

00:27:33.752 --> 00:27:35.151
They've extended the deadline.

00:27:35.220 --> 00:27:38.121
You'll have enough time
to dismantle your equipment.

00:27:38.189 --> 00:27:41.647
Thanks, but there's too much
to take with us.

00:27:41.726 --> 00:27:44.923
Captain Janeway has agreed
to ferry all of you

00:27:45.063 --> 00:27:48.464
and your supplies
to the nearest M-Class planet.

00:27:54.639 --> 00:27:56.937
Come on, Brax.
We're going home.

00:27:57.042 --> 00:27:57.940
Why?

00:27:58.076 --> 00:27:59.873
We have to pack.

00:27:59.944 --> 00:28:01.377
Come on.

00:28:05.083 --> 00:28:07.711
You said you were gonna help us.

00:28:07.786 --> 00:28:08.980
Brax.

00:28:24.969 --> 00:28:26.402
You wanted to see me?

00:28:26.471 --> 00:28:29.702
I've detected five
warp-capable species

00:28:29.774 --> 00:28:31.332
within two light-years
of the planet

00:28:31.409 --> 00:28:32.842
where we're taking
the Talaxians.

00:28:32.911 --> 00:28:35.903
I'm worried they might be
vulnerable to attack.

00:28:35.980 --> 00:28:38.414
They would be vulnerable
anywhere.

00:28:38.483 --> 00:28:40.075
I thought maybe
you could help me

00:28:40.151 --> 00:28:42.711
devise some defense strategies
for their new home.

00:28:42.787 --> 00:28:44.152
Frankly, Mr. Neelix,

00:28:44.222 --> 00:28:47.555
they don't seem inclined
to defend themselves.

00:28:47.625 --> 00:28:49.593
No, I-I suppose not...

00:28:49.661 --> 00:28:51.925
But if they were going
to make a stand,

00:28:52.063 --> 00:28:55.089
their emotional attachment
to their present home

00:28:55.166 --> 00:28:57.430
might be an asset.

00:28:57.502 --> 00:28:59.936
Are you saying they should stay?

00:29:00.004 --> 00:29:02.404
I'm speaking hypothetically.

00:29:02.474 --> 00:29:04.874
"Hypothetically..."

00:29:05.009 --> 00:29:07.273
if they wanted to defend
the asteroid,

00:29:07.345 --> 00:29:08.869
how would they do it?

00:29:09.013 --> 00:29:10.344
To begin with,

00:29:10.415 --> 00:29:13.748
they would need to establish
some kind of perimeter.

00:29:13.818 --> 00:29:16.286
You mean shields?

00:29:16.354 --> 00:29:17.582
Yes.

00:29:17.655 --> 00:29:19.589
The miners are monitoring
the asteroid.

00:29:19.657 --> 00:29:22.091
If they detected the Talaxians
erecting a shield,

00:29:22.160 --> 00:29:23.787
they would attempt to stop them.

00:29:23.862 --> 00:29:25.830
I suppose so.

00:29:25.897 --> 00:29:27.228
Your people

00:29:27.298 --> 00:29:29.425
would need competent leadership
to defend against

00:29:29.501 --> 00:29:32.299
a preemptive attack.

00:29:32.370 --> 00:29:34.304
If you had
the Captain's permission,

00:29:34.372 --> 00:29:37.068
would you be willing
to provide that leadership?

00:29:37.142 --> 00:29:38.404
Certainly not.

00:29:38.476 --> 00:29:40.910
It would be a violation
of the Prime Directive.

00:29:41.045 --> 00:29:42.478
And even if it weren't,

00:29:42.547 --> 00:29:45.641
I don't believe that I am
the person most qualified

00:29:45.717 --> 00:29:47.810
to assume that role.

00:29:49.220 --> 00:29:50.312
You mean me?

00:29:50.388 --> 00:29:53.687
I am merely speaking
hypothetically.

00:29:58.563 --> 00:30:02.932
I couldn't lead those people,
Mr. Tuvok.

00:30:03.067 --> 00:30:05.934
I'm not a fighter.

00:30:06.070 --> 00:30:07.935
I'm just a cook...

00:30:08.072 --> 00:30:11.667
who sometimes imagines himself
to be a diplomat.

00:30:11.743 --> 00:30:15.179
On the contrary,
Mr. Neelix...

00:30:15.246 --> 00:30:18.841
you are much more than that.

00:30:18.917 --> 00:30:21.351
You are perhaps
the most resourceful individual

00:30:21.419 --> 00:30:24.354
I have ever known.

00:30:24.422 --> 00:30:26.754
I always thought you
just tolerated me.

00:30:26.825 --> 00:30:30.522
You do have
some annoying habits.

00:30:30.595 --> 00:30:34.361
However,
during your time on Voyager,

00:30:34.432 --> 00:30:36.957
you've developed
many valuable skills...

00:30:37.068 --> 00:30:38.160
skills that would

00:30:38.236 --> 00:30:39.965
serve you well
if you ever decided

00:30:40.104 --> 00:30:42.971
to assume a leadership role.

00:30:43.107 --> 00:30:45.098
You really think so?

00:30:45.176 --> 00:30:46.973
Let me be clear.

00:30:47.111 --> 00:30:49.807
I'm not urging you
to do anything.

00:30:49.881 --> 00:30:51.473
I am simply telling you

00:30:51.549 --> 00:30:54.609
that I believe
that you are more than capable.

00:31:05.897 --> 00:31:08.331
Going somewhere, Mr. Neelix?

00:31:08.399 --> 00:31:09.525
Just to see my friends.

00:31:09.601 --> 00:31:11.626
Chakotay tells me you're
using your own ship.

00:31:11.703 --> 00:31:13.500
Why not have Tom
take you in the Flyer?

00:31:13.571 --> 00:31:15.163
I didn't want to bother anyone.

00:31:15.240 --> 00:31:17.800
You wouldn't be planning
anything foolish, would you?

00:31:17.876 --> 00:31:20.936
Whatever I do, I promise
it won't involve Voyager.

00:31:21.012 --> 00:31:23.810
That wasn't my question.

00:31:23.882 --> 00:31:27.841
I know you have
Prime Directive issues,

00:31:27.919 --> 00:31:29.716
but I'm not officially
part of your crew,

00:31:29.787 --> 00:31:31.482
so I don't have
the same constraints.

00:31:31.556 --> 00:31:34.582
You're as much a part
of this crew as anyone else.

00:31:35.994 --> 00:31:37.689
Are you ordering me not to go?

00:31:37.762 --> 00:31:39.662
That depends on what
you're going to do.

00:31:41.432 --> 00:31:43.366
It's up to the Talaxians.

00:31:52.710 --> 00:31:55.679
Safe journey, Mr. Neelix.

00:32:05.189 --> 00:32:07.089
I know from personal experience

00:32:07.158 --> 00:32:09.319
that you have
force field emitters.

00:32:09.394 --> 00:32:12.921
We could use them
to establish a shield grid.

00:32:12.997 --> 00:32:15.795
We'd need to deploy
a series of them

00:32:15.867 --> 00:32:19.928
on the asteroid's surface,
along bisecting diameters.

00:32:20.071 --> 00:32:22.767
16 emitters should be enough
to form a grid.

00:32:22.840 --> 00:32:24.307
Even if you're right,

00:32:24.375 --> 00:32:27.037
it'd take weeks to dig that
many tunnels to the surface.

00:32:27.111 --> 00:32:28.271
Commander Tuvok suggested

00:32:28.346 --> 00:32:29.904
that we could
modify the emitters,

00:32:29.981 --> 00:32:31.949
so they could be fired
from torpedo tubes

00:32:32.083 --> 00:32:35.678
on your ship... implanted
in the surface.

00:32:35.753 --> 00:32:37.550
As soon as the miners

00:32:37.622 --> 00:32:39.613
realized what we were doing,
they'd attack.

00:32:39.691 --> 00:32:41.318
I could provide cover
from my ship.

00:32:41.392 --> 00:32:43.587
But you're right,
we'd have to work quickly.

00:32:43.661 --> 00:32:45.185
We could route power
to the emitters

00:32:45.263 --> 00:32:46.389
directly from the core.

00:32:46.464 --> 00:32:47.931
They have
a permanent energy supply.

00:32:47.999 --> 00:32:49.125
Good idea.

00:32:49.200 --> 00:32:51.668
If we do what you're suggesting,
people are going to be hurt.

00:32:51.736 --> 00:32:54.705
This is your home.

00:32:56.040 --> 00:32:59.134
The miners have no right
to force you out.

00:32:59.210 --> 00:33:00.677
I agree,

00:33:00.745 --> 00:33:02.610
- but fighting?
- I don't like it, either,

00:33:02.680 --> 00:33:04.910
but at some point you have
to stand up for yourselves.

00:33:05.016 --> 00:33:08.042
How do you know
there won't be someone else

00:33:08.119 --> 00:33:10.110
to terrorize you
the next place you go?!

00:33:11.222 --> 00:33:12.484
You know he's right.

00:33:15.893 --> 00:33:18.828
No one has worked harder
to build this place than you.

00:33:18.896 --> 00:33:21.694
Isn't it worth defending?

00:33:33.578 --> 00:33:34.909
Wait for my com call.

00:33:34.979 --> 00:33:37.413
As soon as
the last emitter's in place,

00:33:37.482 --> 00:33:39.507
start routing power
to the grid.

00:33:39.584 --> 00:33:41.552
Understood.

00:33:43.588 --> 00:33:45.715
You're scared, aren't you?

00:33:47.859 --> 00:33:49.793
You?

00:33:49.861 --> 00:33:51.624
Terrified.

00:33:51.696 --> 00:33:52.788
Be careful.

00:33:52.864 --> 00:33:54.957
I will.

00:33:55.033 --> 00:33:56.796
Oxilon to Neelix.

00:33:56.868 --> 00:33:58.301
The emitters are loaded.

00:33:58.369 --> 00:34:00.303
We're ready.

00:34:00.371 --> 00:34:02.669
I'll see you soon.

00:34:32.603 --> 00:34:33.729
Two more, and we're done.

00:34:33.805 --> 00:34:35.067
Acknowledged.

00:34:35.139 --> 00:34:38.165
We're moving into position
for the next one.

00:34:40.211 --> 00:34:42.475
The miners' ship
is on an intercept course.

00:34:42.547 --> 00:34:44.344
Evasive maneuvers!

00:34:50.488 --> 00:34:51.648
They're targeting our shields.

00:34:51.722 --> 00:34:52.814
I'll deal with them.

00:34:52.890 --> 00:34:55.882
Just focus on your job.

00:34:55.960 --> 00:34:58.952
All right, Mr. Vulcan, let's see
if you were right about me.

00:35:12.510 --> 00:35:14.444
Neelix, you have to hurry.

00:35:14.512 --> 00:35:17.538
Just one more emitter,
and you can activate the shield.

00:35:28.192 --> 00:35:29.318
Neelix to Oxilon.

00:35:29.393 --> 00:35:30.792
My weapons are off-line.

00:35:30.862 --> 00:35:31.920
We're not in position yet.

00:35:32.029 --> 00:35:33.121
You have to get there.

00:35:33.197 --> 00:35:35.495
They're going
to launch another charge.

00:35:42.340 --> 00:35:43.932
Neelix, what are you doing?

00:35:44.008 --> 00:35:45.441
Don't worry about me.

00:35:45.510 --> 00:35:47.944
Just get ready
to bring the grid on line.

00:35:56.387 --> 00:35:57.854
Delta Flyer to Neelix.

00:35:57.922 --> 00:35:59.321
Are you all right?

00:35:59.390 --> 00:36:02.484
Fine, Captain,
but you shouldn't be here.

00:36:02.560 --> 00:36:04.425
You're violating
the Prime Directive.

00:36:04.495 --> 00:36:06.963
We're just helping
a friend in distress.

00:36:23.080 --> 00:36:24.672
Dexa to Neelix.

00:36:24.749 --> 00:36:26.114
The shield's holding.

00:36:26.184 --> 00:36:27.310
You did it.

00:36:27.385 --> 00:36:30.650
We did it.

00:36:31.722 --> 00:36:35.123
Captain's Log, Stardate 54868.6.

00:36:35.193 --> 00:36:37.252
Commander Nocona
seems to have given up

00:36:37.328 --> 00:36:40.126
his attempts to penetrate
the Talaxians' shield.

00:36:40.198 --> 00:36:41.927
Voyager's ready
to get underway,

00:36:42.033 --> 00:36:43.933
but we're giving
Mr. Neelix time

00:36:44.001 --> 00:36:46.663
to say a difficult good-bye
to his new friends.

00:36:46.737 --> 00:36:48.932
We're grateful
for everything you've done.

00:36:49.006 --> 00:36:51.133
I'm just happy
things worked out.

00:36:51.209 --> 00:36:54.406
And I'm glad that I could
spend some time here...

00:36:54.478 --> 00:36:55.775
with all of you.

00:36:56.981 --> 00:36:57.913
I'd better go.

00:36:57.982 --> 00:36:59.244
Stay here.

00:36:59.317 --> 00:37:01.581
He can't, Brax.

00:37:01.652 --> 00:37:04.212
He has responsibilities
on Voyager.

00:37:04.288 --> 00:37:06.950
I promise I'll stay
in touch as long as I can.

00:37:28.613 --> 00:37:30.581
Come in.

00:37:34.285 --> 00:37:36.685
Hi.

00:37:36.754 --> 00:37:38.722
Neelix.

00:37:40.891 --> 00:37:43.451
What are you working on?

00:37:43.527 --> 00:37:46.087
A report on proto-humanoid
cultures...

00:37:46.163 --> 00:37:49.394
for Commander Chakotay's
paleontology class.

00:37:49.467 --> 00:37:51.059
Aha.

00:37:51.135 --> 00:37:53.069
Need some help?

00:37:53.137 --> 00:37:54.832
I'm almost finished.

00:37:57.074 --> 00:37:59.702
Do you have time
for a game of Kadis-Kot?

00:37:59.777 --> 00:38:02.007
I have to get up early.

00:38:04.115 --> 00:38:06.447
I guess you'd better get
to sleep then.

00:38:08.319 --> 00:38:10.082
Do you want me to tuck you in?

00:38:10.154 --> 00:38:11.678
Tell you a bedtime story?

00:38:12.757 --> 00:38:14.691
You haven't done that in years.

00:38:14.759 --> 00:38:18.251
Just think of all the stories
you've missed.

00:38:18.329 --> 00:38:22.561
Thanks, Neelix,
but I can put myself to bed.

00:38:22.633 --> 00:38:26.228
I'm not a little girl anymore.

00:38:42.019 --> 00:38:45.455
I didn't think anyone else
stayed up this late.

00:38:46.991 --> 00:38:50.825
Well, I wouldn't want you
to have coffee all by yourself.

00:38:50.895 --> 00:38:53.159
Have a seat.

00:39:02.473 --> 00:39:04.532
I've been thinking
about something.

00:39:07.011 --> 00:39:09.673
It's a little hard
to put into words.

00:39:09.747 --> 00:39:12.238
I haven't really made
a decision yet,

00:39:12.316 --> 00:39:13.647
and of course,

00:39:13.718 --> 00:39:17.654
I would never ignore
my responsibilities on Voyager.

00:39:17.722 --> 00:39:19.451
Of course not.

00:39:19.523 --> 00:39:21.650
I take them very seriously.

00:39:21.726 --> 00:39:23.660
I know you do.

00:39:26.530 --> 00:39:29.397
I've been thinking
about something, too.

00:39:29.467 --> 00:39:31.492
Maybe you could help me.

00:39:31.569 --> 00:39:34.163
I'd be happy to.

00:39:34.238 --> 00:39:39.471
It's an idea I'd need to talk
to Starfleet Command about.

00:39:39.543 --> 00:39:41.909
It must be important.

00:39:42.012 --> 00:39:43.912
It is.

00:39:44.014 --> 00:39:45.447
Now that we've established

00:39:45.516 --> 00:39:47.746
two-way communication
with Earth...

00:39:49.987 --> 00:39:53.047
it seems to me Starfleet
could use a permanent Ambassador

00:39:53.124 --> 00:39:55.058
in the Delta Quadrant.

00:39:55.126 --> 00:39:57.560
This ambassador
would have to stay

00:39:57.628 --> 00:40:00.153
in frequent contact
with Voyager.

00:40:00.231 --> 00:40:02.699
Certainly.

00:40:04.802 --> 00:40:06.667
It would be difficult for me
to run this ship

00:40:06.737 --> 00:40:09.069
without you, Neelix.

00:40:09.140 --> 00:40:14.043
But that might be a sacrifice
I'd be willing to make...

00:40:14.111 --> 00:40:17.945
for the greater good
of Starfleet.

00:40:18.015 --> 00:40:21.678
Of course, the assignment
would be entirely voluntary.

00:40:24.388 --> 00:40:28.324
You wouldn't be interested,
would you?

00:41:36.293 --> 00:41:38.625
Good-bye...

00:41:38.696 --> 00:41:41.426
and good luck, Ambassador.

00:41:52.843 --> 00:41:54.640
Mr. Neelix.

00:42:06.323 --> 00:42:09.417
Live long and prosper.
